# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so anything left here is baked into the
# image. Keep this list to things the running service does not need.
#
# Do NOT exclude app/: it is the service. db/schema.sql is already outside this
# build context (it lives in the repo root) and the `migrate` compose service
# mounts it, so nothing here affects migrations.

# Local secrets. The container's environment comes from docker-compose, and
# nothing in app/ reads a dotenv file -- every setting is os.environ.get, so
# excluding these changes no behaviour. It does keep SECRET_KEY out of an
# image layer, where `docker run --entrypoint cat <image> /app/.env.local`
# would hand anyone the key that signs every access token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A local virtualenv is built for the host OS and architecture. Copied into a
# linux image it is both useless and by far the largest thing in the context
# (~183 MB here); pip installs the real dependencies from requirements.txt.
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Python build artefacts and caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The suite cannot run inside the image regardless: tests/conftest.py reads
# db/schema.sql from the repo root, which is outside this build context, and
# its default TEST_DATABASE_URL is localhost:5434 -- a host port that is not
# reachable from inside a container. Shipping the tests anyway would only
# invite someone to "fix" that by pointing TEST_DATABASE_URL at the compose
# database, and the flow fixtures TRUNCATE every table they touch. Run the
# suite on the host against a scratch database instead.
tests/
pytest.ini

# Editor and OS cruft.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Not used at runtime.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
